{"sha":"8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MjMyNTI5ODo4YjUxZGM3MjkxNDczMDkzYzgyMTE5NWM0YjZhZjg1ZmFkZWRiYzJm","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hui Peng","email":"benquike@gmail.com","date":"2019-08-19T22:02:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"Kalle Valo","email":"kvalo@codeaurora.org","date":"2019-09-03T13:54:48Z"},"message":"rsi: fix a double free bug in rsi_91x_deinit()\n\n`dev` (struct rsi_91x_usbdev *) field of adapter\n(struct rsi_91x_usbdev *) is allocated  and initialized in\n`rsi_init_usb_interface`. If any error is detected in information\nread from the device side,  `rsi_init_usb_interface` will be\nfreed. However, in the higher level error handling code in\n`rsi_probe`, if error is detected, `rsi_91x_deinit` is called\nagain, in which `dev` will be freed again, resulting double free.\n\nThis patch fixes the double free by removing the free operation on\n`dev` in `rsi_init_usb_interface`, because `rsi_91x_deinit` is also\nused in `rsi_disconnect`, in that code path, the `dev` field is not\n (and thus needs to be) freed.\n\nThis bug was found in v4.19, but is also present in the latest version\nof kernel. Fixes CVE-2019-15504.\n\nReported-by: Hui Peng <benquike@gmail.com>\nReported-by: Mathias Payer <mathias.payer@nebelwelt.net>\nSigned-off-by: Hui Peng <benquike@gmail.com>\nReviewed-by: Guenter Roeck <linux@roeck-us.net>\nSigned-off-by: Kalle Valo <kvalo@codeaurora.org>","tree":{"sha":"0916f8bcb99e67232241dd779e793b8a8e340c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/0916f8bcb99e67232241dd779e793b8a8e340c58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f/comments","author":{"login":"benquike","id":797426,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NzQyNg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/797426?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike","html_url":"https://github.com/benquike","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benquike/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"13fa451568ab9e8b3074ef741477c7938c713c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/13fa451568ab9e8b3074ef741477c7938c713c42","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/13fa451568ab9e8b3074ef741477c7938c713c42"}],"stats":{"total":1,"additions":0,"deletions":1},"files":[{"sha":"760eaffeebd64a100392f5d97da43ae303428520","filename":"drivers/net/wireless/rsi/rsi_91x_usb.c","status":"modified","additions":0,"deletions":1,"changes":1,"blob_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f/drivers%2Fnet%2Fwireless%2Frsi%2Frsi_91x_usb.c","raw_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/raw/8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f/drivers%2Fnet%2Fwireless%2Frsi%2Frsi_91x_usb.c","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/contents/drivers%2Fnet%2Fwireless%2Frsi%2Frsi_91x_usb.c?ref=8b51dc7291473093c821195c4b6af85fadedbc2f","patch":"@@ -645,7 +645,6 @@ static int rsi_init_usb_interface(struct rsi_hw *adapter,\n \tkfree(rsi_dev->tx_buffer);\n \n fail_eps:\n-\tkfree(rsi_dev);\n \n \treturn status;\n }"}]}